{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"CODE LANDED — Gerrit change 1766 MERGED to main as b6772e4f66 (LLM-Review +1 clean on patch set 2, Verified +1 via CI run 31774466704, no unresolved comments).\n\nAC status:\n- AC3 (contract test): SATISFIED by the landed change — tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/test_normalize_rich_text_contract.py (10 tests) pins normalize_rich_text (None→'', plain str→identity, non-dict→str(), ADF dict→adf_to_text markdown), its (body:Any)->str signature, the InboundMapper protocol exposure, and both JiraBackend/JiraDataCenterBackend .inbound ports delegating identically. Runs in the normal Gerrit/GitHub CI (pytest, all py3.11/3.12/3.13 + macos green). Marked [x].\n\n- AC1 & AC2 (live DC-harness): tagged [operator-attested] because they are verified ONLY by the expensive Dockerized-Jira DC-harness job, which does NOT run on every Gerrit change — it must be OPERATOR-DISPATCHED. NOT self-attested / NOT self-closed.\n\nLive test module (landed): tests/external/live_jira_dc/test_dc_rich_text_live.py — collects+skips cleanly off-harness (absent-harness / absent-extra skip markers), reuses the conftest fixtures (dc_store_copy_repo, dc_transport, bound_dc_issue, jira_dc_project, dc_request) and the session-scoped PAT.\n  * test_live_rich_text_renders_and_echo_is_safe (AC1 + AC2 echo): pushes a heading/bold/code body via rebar.edit_ticket(...)+scoped run_bridge sync, then reads RENDERED HTML via dc_request('/rest/api/2/issue/<key>?expand=renderedFields')->renderedFields.description and asserts: heading (h1.) -> '<h1'; bold (*foo*) -> '<b>' or '<strong>'; code macro ({code}) -> '<pre' or class=\"code\" — each around the run's unique token so it can't pass on a stale doc. Then a SECOND reconcile pass asserts state-based echo-safety: wrote_nothing_problem(...) is None (no re-push; the landed rich body decodes to an unchanged value). _push_and_converge waits for a JQL search to reflect the pushed token before the next pass so the echo pass reads a fresh (not index-lagged) remote.\n  * test_live_rich_text_both_sides_conflict_keeps_local (AC2 conflict): pushes a body and converges to record a baseline (settle pass asserts wrote_nothing), then makes BOTH a rebar-side edit (rebar.edit_ticket description) AND a Jira-side edit (dc_transport.update_issue description) before the next pass, and asserts: rebar's token is the landed description (LOCAL-WINS), the Jira token is NOT present (remote not clobbered), AND alert_store.is_deduped('outbound-field-conflict:<key>:description', repo_root=repo) is True (both-sides divergence surfaced as a deduped bridge alert — remote value recorded, not silently destroyed). Mirrors 3388's test_concurrent_conflict_alerts precondition.\n\nCI wiring (AC1/AC2 dispatch): the module runs in the EXISTING amd64 DC-harness job — no new job. In .github/workflows/external-integration.yml the job is 'jira-dc-harness' (workflow name 'Live External Integration'), which runs 'pytest -m external tests/external/live_jira_dc -q -rA --durations=25' (~line 613); the new module is auto-collected by that directory glob. A note was added just above that step.\n\nOPERATOR ACTION REQUIRED to complete AC1/AC2: dispatch the 'Live External Integration' workflow (.github/workflows/external-integration.yml, job jira-dc-harness) via GitHub Actions workflow_dispatch on the navapbc/rebar repo — e.g. 'gh workflow run \"Live External Integration\" --repo navapbc/rebar --ref main' — which stands up the Dockerized Jira 8.17.1 instance and runs the live rich-text tests. When that job is green, AC1/AC2 are satisfied and the ticket can be closed. Ticket left in_progress until then."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1786689419944393001,"uuid":"e43d6d71-3e06-4193-88ee-ed93a2d01ef9"}